  "description": "SYNC4 (#4255 turn scope on the durable path). Node pins, at admission, the selection the request named below app level (recordGroups, records, recordsExact: sorted, unique, valid ids) and a saved agent's per-source limits (sourceLimits) next to apps/kb/strictScope in x.pipeshub.knowledge; never the expanded node set or any access result. A request with a selection that leaves apps or kb out means none of that kind, never all of the agent's (main's resolve_agent_filters). With internal search off nothing is pinned. A child keeps its parent's selection and limits unchanged and may only narrow apps/kb. Python reads the pin back as the filters it hands main's _resolve_turn_filters / prepare_turn_scope (`requested`), resolving and checking access on every attempt. `pins` cases: Node `grantedKnowledge` (domain/run-spec.ts) and Python `requested_filters` (app/harness/assembly/scope.py). `children` cases: Node `childGrants` then `childRunSpec` (domain/child-runs.ts); the child's pin is read by Python like any other. `feature` is whether the run needs the `knowledge_selection` worker feature (an older worker's strict models would refuse the new fields).",
